{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% import '_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
{% block title %}Observability · Fuzzphony{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<div class="page stack">
    <div class="hero">
        <h1>Observability</h1>
        <p class="lede">Fuzzphony reports every search, sync and reindex operation through a <code>MetricsCollector</code>: nothing, structured log lines, or Prometheus.</p>
        {{ ui.search_field(path('observability'), query, 'catalog', 'Query to measure') }}
    </div>
    <div>{{ ui.examples(examples, 'observability') }}</div>

    <section aria-labelledby="reported">
        <h2 id="reported" class="list-title">What this search reported · <code>{{ query }}</code> · {{ total }} hits</h2>
        <div class="table-card">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Kind</th><th>This run</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.search.took_ms</code></td><td>histogram</td><td>{{ took_ms }} ms</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.search.fallback</code></td><td>counter</td><td>{{ fallback ? '+1 (typo tolerance ran)' : 'not incremented (exact match was enough)' }}</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>SQL statements</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>{{ statements }}</td></tr>
                    {% if queue %}<tr><td><code>fuzzphony.queue.depth</code></td><td>gauge</td><td>{{ queue.message }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="other-half">
        <h2 id="other-half" class="list-title">The other half</h2>
        <p class="callout"><span>Metrics count searches and never say who searched what: the query text is left out on purpose. That is the job of the search log, which keeps the text, the user, the tenant, the outcome and (masked) the client address of each search, and is personal data. See it on the <a href="{{ path('analytics') }}#who">Analytics page, &ldquo;Who searched what&rdquo;</a>.</span></p>
    </section>

    <details class="disclosure">
        <summary>The log lines for it<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg></summary>
        <p class="muted">This demo uses the logging collector (it has neither <code>promphp/prometheus_client_php</code> nor <code>apcu</code>) and writes the lines to the php container's log: <code>docker compose logs -f php</code>. The values are this run's.</p>
        <pre tabindex="0"><code>fuzzphony.metric {"event":"fuzzphony.search.took_ms","value":{{ took_ms }},"index":"catalog"}{% if fallback %}

fuzzphony.metric {"event":"fuzzphony.search.fallback","by":1,"index":"catalog"}{% endif %}</code></pre>
        <p class="muted">The query text is left out of the line unless you opt in (<code>logQueryText</code>), and is never a Prometheus label (one time series per distinct query would never stop growing).</p>
    </details>

    <details class="disclosure">
        <summary>Everything Fuzzphony can report<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg></summary>
        <div class="table-card">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Kind</th><th>From</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.search.took_ms</code></td><td>histogram</td><td>every search</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.search.fallback</code></td><td>counter</td><td>searches that needed typo tolerance</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.&lt;operation&gt;.duration_ms</code> / <code>.errors</code></td><td>histogram / counter</td><td>every engine operation (rebuild, refresh, queue, pruning&hellip;)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.queue.depth</code></td><td>gauge</td><td>the sync worker, once per cycle</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.queue.processed</code></td><td>counter</td><td>the sync worker</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.worker.rebuild_failures</code></td><td>counter</td><td>the sync worker</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>fuzzphony.messenger.refresh.duration_ms</code> / <code>.errors</code></td><td>histogram / counter</td><td>the ORM-sync Messenger handler</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="disclosure">
        <summary>Prometheus and Grafana<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chevron"/></svg></summary>
        <p>The bundle picks the Prometheus collector on its own when <code>promphp/prometheus_client_php</code> is installed and <code>apcu</code> is loaded and enabled in that process, and quietly falls back to logging otherwise. With it the metrics become scrapeable series (expose them with a small <code>/metrics</code> route, see <code>docs/observability.md</code>), and <code>docs/grafana/fuzzphony-overview.json</code> is a ready-made dashboard: search latency and fallback rate, queue depth, errors by operation, and the sync handler. Import it under Dashboards &rarr; New &rarr; Import. <code>fuzzphony:doctor --format=prometheus</code> prints the doctor checks as metrics for node_exporter's textfile collector.</p>
    </details>
</div>
{% endblock %}
